From Thomas.Adams at noaa.gov  Sun Aug 21 18:35:16 2005
From: Thomas.Adams at noaa.gov (Thomas Adams)
Date: Wed Nov 14 16:58:13 2007
Subject: [STATSGRASS] Unable to read GRASS6 data using gstat 2.4.5
Message-ID: <430901A4.3050508@noaa.gov>

List:

I have point temperature data in GRASS6 (as vectors); I'm using GSTAT 
2.4.5 which I have compiled with GRASS support (and confirmed with gstat 
-v). From the GRASS6 prompt, when I try to execute:

gstat gstat.cmd.temps

I get:

gstat: read failed on file 'temp_20050101_08'


where my GSTAT command file (gstat.cmd.temps) is:

# file: gstat.cmd.temps
#
# gstat command file
#
data(temp_20050101_08): 'temp_20050101_08', x=1, y=2, v=1;
variogram(temp_20050101_08): 0.2772 Nug(0) + 0.85 Sph(987521);

Previously, using GRASS 5.4 and GSTAT, this procedure worked, where 
'temp_20050101_08' would be my point data. Obviously, I'm missing 
something; any ideas?

Regards,
Tom


